    <!-- Faceted pentagon "gem" mark for Facet Launcher. Outer pentagon (radius 32) and inner
         pentagon (radius 14, same orientation) define 5 quad panels; each panel is split by
         BOTH of its diagonals (outer vertex to the far inner vertex, each way), crossing at an
         interior point, into 4 triangular facets. Every facet gets its own color: hue sweeps
         continuously by the facet's own centroid angle around the ring (navy -> steel -> gray ->
         teal -> green, matching the design reference), and lightness varies by the facet's role
         within its panel (outer-edge brightest, inner-edge darkest) - so no two facets, including
         ones that share an edge across a panel boundary, ever land on the same color. -->

